// a reference cannot be taken twice - `ptr<T&>` is the spelling for a pointer to a borrow.
//
// note the space: `int&&` lexes as a single logical-and token and never reaches the type parser,
// so only the spaced form produces this diagnostic. the glued form is rejected as an unexpected
// token instead.
//
// the signature is read in every module pass, so this also pins that the issue is reported once
function f(int& & $x) : void {}
